---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { legalAddress, legalCompany, legalMailto } from "../lib/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy — Zenguy"
  description="How NIESAYO GROUP, S.L. processes personal data for Zenguy under the GDPR and Spain’s LOPDGDD."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how {legalCompany.legalName} (“we”, “us”),
    acting under the trade name {legalCompany.tradeName}, processes personal
    data when you use {legalCompany.site}, {legalCompany.app}, the iOS app, or
    related services (browser tests, uptime monitoring, incidents, alerts and
    billing).
  </p>
  <p>
    It is the layered information required by articles 13 and 14 of Regulation
    (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD). It is not a contract
    of adhesion for extra processing: account data needed to provide Zenguy
    rest on the contract; marketing and non-essential cookies rest on separate
    consent.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Controller</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.legalName}</dd>
    <dt>NIF</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.nif}</dd>
    <dt>Address</dt>
    <dd>{legalAddress}</dd>
    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a></dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    We have not appointed a data protection officer because our core activities
    do not require one under article 37 GDPR. You can still write to{" "}
    <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a> for any privacy request.
    You may also complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD),
    {" "}<a href="https://www.aepd.es">www.aepd.es</a>, or to another EU
    supervisory authority where you live or work.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Roles: controller and processor</h2>
  <p>
    For your account, workspace membership, billing, support and security logs,
    we are the <strong>controller</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For personal data that appear inside the sites you ask us to test or
    monitor (for example a name on a checkout screenshot, a customer email in
    a flow, or a secret you store), <strong>you are the controller</strong> and
    we act as your <strong>processor</strong> under article 28 GDPR. You must
    have a lawful basis to involve us, must not send special-category data
    unless strictly necessary and lawful, and must configure tests so they
    avoid unnecessary personal data. Processor terms are in the{" "}
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Data we process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data:</strong> name, email, password hash, verification
      status, legal acceptances (terms, privacy acknowledgement, marketing
      choice and version).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Workspace data:</strong> workspace name, members, roles,
      invitations, settings and time zone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service configuration:</strong> browser-test instructions, start
      URLs, schedules, HTTP monitors, alert channels (email, phone number,
      Slack/Discord webhooks), and encrypted secrets you store.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Run evidence:</strong> logs, screenshots, network diagnostics,
      Markdown failure reports and incident records, retained for 30 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing data:</strong> Stripe customer and subscription
      identifiers, invoices, usage of runs and prepaid alert credit. Card
      details are collected by Stripe, not stored by us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device and security data:</strong> IP address, user agent,
      approximate location derived from IP, session tokens, app version, and
      diagnostic logs needed to secure the service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications:</strong> emails we send (verification, password
      reset, operational alerts, and, if you opt in, product updates) and
      support messages you send us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>iOS app:</strong> Face ID stays on the device (we do not receive
      biometric templates). Push tokens are processed to deliver optional
      notifications you enable.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data. We do not build advertising profiles.</p>

  <h2>4. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <p>Each purpose has its own article 6 GDPR basis:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Create and administer the account, workspaces and the service</strong>
      — performance of the contract (art. 6.1.b). Providing name, email and a
      password is necessary; without them we cannot open an account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Run the tests and monitors you configure, store evidence, and
      send operational alerts to destinations you add</strong>
      — contract (art. 6.1.b). For phone, SMS or WhatsApp destinations we also
      need the recipient’s permission, which you confirm when you create the
      channel (consent, art. 6.1.a, as regards that recipient).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing, invoicing, tax and accounting</strong>
      — contract (art. 6.1.b) and legal obligation (art. 6.1.c), including the
      Spanish Commercial Code and General Tax Law retention duties.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Security, abuse prevention, debugging and service reliability</strong>
      — legitimate interests (art. 6.1.f): keeping the service safe and
      available for you and other customers. You may object under article 21
      GDPR.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Comply with law, respond to authorities, and handle claims</strong>
      — legal obligation (art. 6.1.c) or legitimate interests (art. 6.1.f).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Product emails about Zenguy</strong> (not operational alerts) —
      consent (art. 6.1.a and art. 21 LSSI-CE). The checkbox is optional,
      unchecked by default, and can be withdrawn at any time by writing to{" "}
      <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>. Consent is not a
      condition of creating an account.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not take solely automated decisions with legal or similarly
    significant effects (art. 22 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>5. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>
    We only share data with providers that help us operate Zenguy, under a
    contract, and only as needed:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> and its EEA entity — hosting (Workers,
      Pages), database (D1), object storage (R2), DNS, email sending and
      security.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stripe, Inc. / Stripe Payments Europe, Limited</strong> —
      subscriptions, invoices, tax and the customer portal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Twilio Inc.</strong> — SMS and voice operational alerts you
      configure. We do not share mobile numbers with anyone for their
      marketing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>OpenAI, LLC</strong> — model inference used to drive the browser
      agent that executes your instructions. Do not put secrets in the
      instruction text if you can avoid it; use the secrets vault.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Expo (650 Industries, Inc.)</strong> — iOS push delivery and app
      updates, when you use the iOS app.
    </li>
    <li>
      Slack, Discord or other destinations <em>you</em> choose as alert
      webhooks — those providers then process the message under their terms.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data if required by a court or authority, or to
    professional advisers bound by confidentiality.
  </p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some providers (notably Cloudflare, Stripe, Twilio, OpenAI and Expo) may
    process data in the United States or other countries outside the EEA.
    Where that happens we rely on an adequacy decision, the EU–US Data Privacy
    Framework if the provider is certified, and/or the European Commission’s
    Standard Contractual Clauses, plus supplementary measures where needed
    (GDPR Chapter V).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account and workspace records: while the account is open.</li>
    <li>
      After deletion: we keep billing and tax records for up to six years, as
      Spanish commercial and tax law requires, and security logs for up to
      twelve months unless a claim needs them longer.
    </li>
    <li>Run evidence (screenshots, reports, logs): 30 days.</li>
    <li>Marketing consent records: until you withdraw consent, plus evidence of the consent for the period we may need to demonstrate it (art. 7.1 GDPR).</li>
    <li>
      If you never verify the email, the pending account and its verification
      token expire on the schedule described in the product (verification
      tokens last 24 hours; unverified accounts may be removed as abuse
      prevention).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use TLS, hashed passwords, encrypted secrets, access control by
    workspace role, short-lived sessions, rate limits and audit logs. No
    online service is perfectly secure. If a personal-data breach is likely to
    result in a risk to you, we will notify the AEPD within 72 hours where
    required (art. 33 GDPR) and we will inform you when art. 34 GDPR requires
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability
    and objection, and you may withdraw consent without affecting earlier
    lawful processing (arts. 15–21 GDPR, arts. 12–18 LOPDGDD). You also have
    the right not to be subject to solely automated decisions (art. 22).
  </p>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>. We may need to
    verify your identity. We will answer within one month, extendable as the
    GDPR allows. You can also complain to the AEPD.
  </p>
  <p>
    In Spain, users aged 14 or over may generally consent to information-society
    services (art. 7 LOPDGDD). Zenguy is a business service: the contract
    requires that you are 18 or older and able to bind yourself or your
    organisation.
  </p>

  <h2>10. SMS and phone alerts</h2>
  <p>
    Operational SMS and calls are only sent to numbers you enrol, after an
    explicit, unchecked confirmation in the product. We do not sell mobile
    numbers or SMS opt-in data, and we do not share them with third parties
    for their marketing. Recipients can reply STOP to opt out of SMS from the
    sending number, or HELP for help. Consent to SMS is not a condition of
    buying Zenguy. Frequency follows the monitors you configure and may include
    several messages in a day when something is down.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>Zenguy is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>12. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy when the service or the law changes. The date at
    the top is the current version. Material changes will be announced in the
    product or by email when appropriate. Continued use after the effective
    date of a change that does not require new consent means you have been
    informed of that change.
  </p>
</Legal>
